The patient, Mary Jane Grey, is a 45-year-old female who presents via telemedicine for an emergency consultation due to severe dizziness, nausea, and unsteady gait that began approximately 2 hours ago. The symptoms are continuous and have significantly impacted her ability to walk straight and perform daily tasks. She also reports a mild buzzing in her ears. The patient mentions a similar episode one month ago, which resolved quickly, but this episode has persisted for a longer duration. She denies any recent viral illness or other systemic symptoms.

